<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I957ed746f9d41cec0524b0006847bb74b6310c64" commit="3b4b471882b2816bb179bd02a238d27b30e930e2" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dma-buf/fence: revert &quot;don't wait when specified timeout is zero&quot; (v2)  Reverts commit 847b19a39e4c  (&quot;dma-buf/fence: don't wait when specified timeout is zero&quot;)  When we don't call the wait function software signaling might never be activated. This can cause infinite polling loops with unreliable interrupt driven hardware.  v2: rebase on drm-next  BUG=chromium:762583 TEST=boot up kevin  Reviewed-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Christian Knig &lt;christian.koenig@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chunming Zhou &lt;david1.zhou@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gustavo Padovan &lt;gustavo.padovan@collabora.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt;   [sumits: reword commit msg for checkpatch warnings] Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1478553376-18575-2-git-send-email-alexander.deucher@amd.com (cherry picked from commit 698c0f7ff21674ec08a4c6e99dd6da62fe5a344d) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I957ed746f9d41cec0524b0006847bb74b6310c64 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/754375 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="754375" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/75/754375/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I09895a3607af5537932a09245080ebbe71b16486" commit="5599c1ad78b8e36894941bba1bffbf293aa97850" commit_message="UPSTREAM: reservation: revert &quot;wait only with non-zero timeout specified (v3)&quot; v2  Reverts commit fb8b7d2b9d80  (&quot;reservation: wait only with non-zero timeout specified (v3)&quot;)  Otherwise signaling might never be activated on the fences. This can result in infinite waiting with hardware which has unreliable interrupts.  v2: still return one when the timeout is zero and we don't have any fences.  BUG=chromium:762583 TEST=boot up kevin  Reviewed-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Christian Knig &lt;christian.koenig@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chunming Zhou &lt;david1.zhou@amd.com&gt; (v1) Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gustavo Padovan &lt;gustavo.padovan@collabora.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt;   [sumits: fix checkpatch warnings] Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1478553376-18575-4-git-send-email-alexander.deucher@amd.com (cherry picked from commit 06a66b5c77ede71f0601f4710284ca1076e673fa) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I09895a3607af5537932a09245080ebbe71b16486 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/754376 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="754376" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/76/754376/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5b3cdc81f3d95b48220c03817a7ae52c356c94a1" commit="a267e34ffcb01cedfd3fedcf555703e47a49d02c" commit_message="graphics_VTSwitch: add delay between starting Chrome and screenshot  Add 10 second delay before screenshot is taken. It may take a while for Chrome to start and switch video mode and show someth